## 2. What challenges did you face in your last project, and how did you resolve them?

→ **Challenge 1 — Duplicate Kafka events:** The same event could be delivered more than once. I used idempotent processing and event identifiers to prevent duplicate business updates.

→ **Challenge 2 — Out-of-order events:** Older laboratory results could arrive after newer results. I used result versioning and validation to prevent stale updates from replacing newer data.

→ **Challenge 3 — Concurrent database updates:** Multiple requests could update the same result simultaneously. I used optimistic locking with a version field to detect conflicts.

→ **Challenge 4 — Performance and production issues:** I worked on resolving N+1 queries, investigating Kafka consumer lag, and troubleshooting notification failures using logs and monitoring.

